---GroupBoxes are similar to Layers, allowing components to be arbitrarily positioned and sized within them. Unlike
---other layout components however, groupboxes also contain some visual elements, namely a background sprite enclosing
---the component's contents, and an optional header section composed of a sprite and a label.
---
---This makes groupboxes ideal for situations where you'd like to make it clear some UI elements are grouped or
---categorised together, or to highlight a section of an interface. They are also a good component container to use when
---creating a new interface since otherwise you would usually need to create and manage a separate background element.
---@class ui.GroupBox : ui.ComponentCollection
---@field headerWidth integer The header's width in interface units.
---@field headerHeight integer The header's height in interface units.
---@field headerOffsetX integer The header's offset from the left in interface units.
---@field headerOffsetY integer The header's offset from the right in interface units.
---@field headerAlignment ui.GroupBoxHeaderAlignMode Defines how the header should be positioned.
---@field headerText any (Modifiable Contents) Label properties used for the header text.
---@field contentBackgroundSprite ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the background.
---@field headerBackgroundSprite ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the header background.
---@field contentMargin ui.Margin (Modifiable Contents) Offsets used to determine the inner content area for this component.
ui.GroupBox = {}

---Creates a new GroupBox on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this groupbox in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.GroupBox # The newly created groupbox. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.GroupBox.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Sets the parameters used to position and size the component's header area.
---
---Warning: Make sure your component's contents still fit when using a header, since the available height for content
---will be reduced based on the header's height and vertical offset.
---@param width integer The header's width in interface units.
---@param height integer The header's height in interface units.
---@param offsetX integer The header's offset from the left in interface units.
---@param offsetY integer The header's offset from the right in interface units.
---@param alignment ui.GroupBoxHeaderAlignMode Defines how the header should be positioned.
function ui.GroupBox:SetHeaderLayout(width, height, offsetX, offsetY, alignment) end

---Specifies how the groupbox header will be positioned horizontally.
---
---Info: Headers are always positioned at the top of the component regardless of alignment.
---@class ui.GroupBoxHeaderAlignMode
---@field LEFT ui.GroupBoxHeaderAlignMode The header is positioned against the left side of the component.
---@field CENTRE ui.GroupBoxHeaderAlignMode The header is centred on the component.
---@field RIGHT ui.GroupBoxHeaderAlignMode The header is positioned against the right side of the component.
ui.GroupBoxHeaderAlignMode = {}
